FADE IN:

EXT. ABANDONED WAREHOUSE - NIGHT

Rain pounds the cracked asphalt. Lightning illuminates the skeletal remains of industrial buildings.

                                     SARAH CONNOR
                         (into radio)
                    All units, we have a problem.

                                     SARAH CONNOR (CONT'D)
                    The target is not where intel said 
                    it would be.

INT. WAREHOUSE - CONTINUOUS

Sarah moves through shadows, weapon drawn. Every footstep echoes.

                                     VOICE (O.S.)
                    Looking for someone?

Sarah spins around. Nothing.

                                     SARAH CONNOR
                         (whispered)
                    Show yourself.

A figure emerges from behind rusted machinery.

                                     MARCUS STEEL
                    You're too late, Connor.

                                     SARAH CONNOR
                    It's never too late to do the right 
                    thing.

                                     MARCUS STEEL
                         (laughing coldly)
                    Right thing? You destroyed everything 
                    I worked for.

Marcus pulls out a detonator.

                                     MARCUS STEEL (CONT'D)
                    Now it's my turn.

                                     SARAH CONNOR
                    Wait! There are innocent people in 
                    the building next door.

                                     MARCUS STEEL
                         (pause)
                    Sometimes sacrifices must be made.

Thunder CRASHES outside. Sarah notices a red light blinking on a nearby device.

                                     SARAH CONNOR
                    You've already activated it.

                                     MARCUS STEEL
                    Five minutes. That should give you 
                    just enough time to run.

                                     SARAH CONNOR
                    I'm not running.

She drops her weapon and steps closer.

                                     SARAH CONNOR (CONT'D)
                    But I'm also not fighting you anymore.

Marcus hesitates, finger hovering over the detonator.

                                     MARCUS STEEL
                    What are you doing?

                                     SARAH CONNOR
                    Something I should have done years ago.
                         (beat)
                    I'm sorry, Marcus. For everything.

The red light blinks faster. Time is running out.

                                     MARCUS STEEL
                         (softening)
                    Sarah...

                                     SARAH CONNOR
                    Help me stop this. Help me save them.

Marcus looks at the detonator, then at Sarah. The weight of his choices shows in his eyes.

                                     MARCUS STEEL
                         (after a long pause)
                    The abort code is... 7749.

Sarah rushes to the device and enters the code. The red light stops blinking.

                                     SARAH CONNOR
                         (relieved)
                    Thank you.

                                     MARCUS STEEL
                    Don't thank me yet. This was just 
                    the backup. The real device is in 
                    the building next door.

Sarah's eyes widen.

                                     SARAH CONNOR
                    How much time?

                                     MARCUS STEEL
                    Two minutes. Maybe less.

They look at each other. Former enemies now united by necessity.

                                     SARAH CONNOR
                    Then we better run.

They sprint toward the exit as lightning flashes again.

                                                    CUT TO:

EXT. WAREHOUSE DISTRICT - CONTINUOUS

Sarah and Marcus burst through the warehouse doors, running toward the adjacent building.

                                     MARCUS STEEL
                         (shouting over rain)
                    Service entrance! Around back!

They disappear around the corner as sirens wail in the distance.

                                                    FADE OUT.

THE END